    "explanation": "Both parties accept the key timing facts, and they decide this case. The driver did arrive and was stationary inside the large-venue pickup geofence: EV-GPS-09103 shows 25 consecutive in-geofence fixes from 17:15:00 to 17:19:00, all about 24.0 m from the pin and inside the 120 m arrival radius, so the arrival conditions in POL-NS-02 are met. But POL-NS-01 requires a continuous in-geofence hold of at least the fee-schedule minimum of 300 seconds for a LARGE_VENUE pickup, measured from the first qualifying fix and not from the arrived marker. The first qualifying fix is at 17:15:00 and the trip was cancelled at 17:19:00, giving a dwell of 240 seconds. That is 60 seconds short, so POL-NS-01 limb (c) fails. The shortfall is even larger if measured from the driver's 17:15:20 arrived marker (about 220 seconds). POL-NS-06 then applies: where the effective in-geofence dwell is below the minimum for the zone class, the cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present or responded. The fee charged was SGD 8.00, correctly calculated as the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_XL vehicle-tier fee (SGD 8.00), but the full SGD 8.00 must be returned. No driver compensation is payable because POL-NS-06 displaces POL-NS-07; the driver's good faith and stationary hold do not change the dwell requirement. There is no false-arrival referral under POL-NS-05(ii), because qualifying in-geofence fixes do exist, and no POL-NS-03 wrong-entrance or pin-ambiguity payment applies, because the driver was inside the arrival radius and there was only one registered pickup point. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09103-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0), but it is not needed: POL-NS-06 limb (i) is unavailable and the trace shows only one in-geofence interval, so accumulation cannot cure the shortfall. No POL-NS-08 impairment applies: there is no clock skew, no trace gap, the chat log matches trip_record.chat_message_count and has no message-numbering hole, and the SGD 8.00 fare line reconciles with the resolution rule. No POL-NS-09 escalation is engaged: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, the evidence is consistent, and no anti-farming or repeat-dispute trigger is met. The rider's absence and non-response are noted but, under POL-NS-06, do not defeat the refund."
