    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "The SGD 8.00 XL cancellation fee does not stand and is refunded to the rider in full.\n\nWhy the fee fails. A no-show fee is chargeable under POL-NS-01 only if, among other conditions, the driver held position inside the pickup geofence for a continuous dwell of at least the fee-schedule minimum for the zone class - 300 seconds for a LARGE_VENUE pickup. The platform's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-09103, weight 1.0) places the driver inside the 120 m arrival radius, at 24.0 m from the recorded bay pin, stationary at 0.0 km/h, for a single continuous in-geofence run of 240 seconds (first qualifying fix 17:15:00, last fix 17:19:00, 25 qualifying fixes). That is 60 seconds short of the 300-second minimum. The trip record (EV-TRIP-09103, weight 1.0) confirms the same window: the driver marked arrival at 17:15:20 and cancelled at 17:19:00 under reason RIDER_NO_SHOW. POL-NS-01 limb (c) therefore fails, and limb (d) fails too, because termination came before the required dwell could elapse. Because the effective in-geofence dwell is shorter than the minimum, POL-NS-06 requires the cancellation fee to be refunded in full, 'whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded to messages.' The rider was charged SGD 8.00 and SGD 0.00 has been refunded (EV-FARE-09103); the whole SGD 8.00 falls to be returned.\n\nNo driver compensation. POL-NS-07 compensates the driver at 80 percent only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it. POL-NS-06 displaces it here, so no compensation is payable. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip in any event: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (below the four-termination trigger) and 1 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 120 is 0.008 (far below 0.08), and these are the only two fields that check reads.\n\nPoints that do not change the outcome, answered together. (1) The driver did arrive and did hold honestly: the trace puts him well inside the arrival radius (POL-NS-02 satisfied), and POL-NS-05 does not bite - at the 17:15:20 arrival marker he was 24.0 m from the pin and stationary, not more than 300 m away and not travelling at 15 km/h or above - so no false-arrival finding or referral arises. The refund is owed because the hold fell 60 seconds short, not because of any misconduct. (2) POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance / pin ambiguity) has no application: the driver was inside the 120 m radius on every fix, and trip_record.registered_pickup_points is 1, so no pin-ambiguity goodwill is computed. (3) POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider - there is no rider locating message in the chat log and 0 of the rider's 11 fixes fall within the 150 m rider-presence radius, the rider's device sitting about 519 m from the pin - but that is immaterial, because POL-NS-06 refunds a dwell shortfall regardless of rider presence or response. (4) The SGD 8.00 figure itself is correct: under the resolution rule it is the greater of the SGD 4.00 LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee and the SGD 8.00 RYDE_XL vehicle-tier fee, which is exactly the cancellation-fee line in the fare breakdown, so there is no fare defect and the refund is the full SGD 8.00 rather than a reduction of it.\n\nEvidence integrity and escalation. No artifact in the bundle is impaired for policy purposes under POL-NS-08: there is no clock skew (the 17:15:20 marker and the 17:19:00 cancellation each coincide with a trace fix), no trace defect (25 fixes, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0, rider track present), no chat defect (the 3 logged messages match trip_record.chat_message_count of 3, with no numbering hole and no gap over 5 minutes), and no fare defect. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or presence, neither party's disputes_with_counterparty_90d is above 0, the anti-farming check is not tripped, rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and the deciding evidence is not impaired. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09103-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) and is not relied on by this ruling. No referral is produced by any clause.\n\nProfile fields. Both sides mentioned the lifetime counters prior_no_show_flags (driver 2, rider 1). POL-GEN-01 makes those context only and neither side used them as a ground of decision, so no claim turns on them and they carry no adverse finding here.",
    "case_no": 9103
  },
